# Win32_EncryptableVolume's answers, in the form
# faraday_starter_shell::windows::bitlocker::Recorded reads, made by hand to
# the class's documented methods and return values (`faraday-starter
# --record-bitlocker` on a Windows computer prints the same form, with no
# recovery password in it). The volumes, IDs and keys are made up.
#
# Two Windows installations, C: and E:. C: suspends; E: is refused, so C:
# is resumed again and nothing is left half done.
volume \\?\Volume{1b2c3d4e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c}\ C: type 0 protection 1
volume \\?\Volume{1b2c3d4e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e}\ E: type 0 protection 1
call \\?\Volume{1b2c3d4e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c}\ DisableKeyProtectors DisableCount=u32:0 -> 0
call \\?\Volume{1b2c3d4e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e}\ DisableKeyProtectors DisableCount=u32:0 -> 2150694970
call \\?\Volume{1b2c3d4e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c}\ EnableKeyProtectors -> 0
